.policy "ruff-ann201-missing-return-type-undocumented-public-function" revision 2
.description "Add a return type annotation to public functions and methods so callers and type checkers know what they return."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff ANN201 (flake8-annotations): a public function or method with no return annotation. Public is Ruff's
// visibility: the name has no leading underscore, nor has any class or module around it; a def inside a def is
// never public; with `__all__`, a top-level def must be listed in it. Class, static and dunder methods have
// their own codes (ANN206, ANN205, ANN204); the implementation after an @overload is not checked. Ruff's
// option suppress-none-returning is not supported (its default, false, is what this rule does).
//   def foo(a: int): ...             ← ANN201
//   class C:
//       def pub(self): ...          ← ANN201
//   def _helper(): ...              not reported here: private (ANN202)
#include "python/annotations.rr"

.violation ANN201(at: node, name: symbol) code "ANN201"
    "Add a return type annotation to `{name}` (for example `-> None` if it returns nothing)."
    suppress ruff "ANN201"
ANN201(nm, x) :- ann_missing_return(f, "ANN201"), field(f, "name", nm), text(nm, x).
